<title>AUSTRALIA: RALLYING-AUSTRALIAN RALLY FINAL STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>RALLYING-AUSTRALIAN RALLY FINAL STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>PERTH, Australia 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading standings after</p>
<p>the third and final day of the Rally of Australia on Monday:</p>
<p> 1. Tommi Makinen (Finland) Mitsubishi Lancer   4 hours 8</p>
<p>minutes 50 seconds</p>
<p> 2. Kenneth Eriksson (Sweden) Subaru Impreza    one minute 17</p>
<p>seconds behind</p>
<p> 3. Carlos Sainz (Spain) Ford Escort		    1:21</p>
<p> 4. Colin McRae (Britain) Subaru Impreza		3:11</p>
<p> 5. Richard Burns (Britain) Mitsubishi Lancer	 3:23</p>
<p> 6. Bruno Thiry (Belgium) Ford Escort		   8:48</p>
<p> 7. Piero Liatti (Italy) Subaru Impreza		11:31</p>
<p> 8. Possum Bourne (New Zealand) Subaru Impreza     12:07</p>
<p> 9. Uwe Nittel (Germany) Mitsubishi Lancer	   23:59</p>
<p> 10. Yoshio Fujimoto (Japan) Toyota Celica	   27:12</p>
<p>World championship standings (after seven of nine races):</p>
<p> 1. Makinen				 115 points</p>
<p> 2. Sainz				    74</p>
<p> 3. Eriksson				 66</p>
<p> 4. McRae				    52</p>
<p> 5. Liatti				   41</p>
</text>
